<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; Provisional machine alignment by Codex (Tibetan-first independent proposal). Original GMR English and ACIP-derived Wylie preserved. thams cad owns the first each and every; the resumed each one of them is unclaimed. lo re re is omitted because yearly recurrence is recast across the following seasonal wording without a separately defensible year exponent. dus tshigs owns the HGM-attested compound four seasons; zhag re rer is the complete distributive phrase day by day, with yang separately even. nyams owns get worse and 'bri the repeated less and less. Articles, participants, auxiliaries, ever manage to find, and the framing words around seasons/month stay unwrapped. No uncertain correspondence is nulled. This is a proposal, not human-approved correspondence.</div>
